<title>BELGIUM: EU to clear Coca-Cola British deal--EU source.</title>
<headline>EU to clear Coca-Cola British deal--EU source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is expected to clear the acquisition by Coca-Cola Enterprises Inc of Cadbury Schweppes' 51 percent stake in British bottler CCSB later this month, a European Union source said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Although the Commission's merger task force initially concluded that the deal could affect fair competition in Britain, it had been unable to substaniate its concerns, the source said.</p>
<p>&quot;We knew that argument was shaky and the legal service had doubts of its own,&quot; the source told Reuters.</p>
<p>The source declined to elaborate but an EU anti-trust expert also hinted that a meeting of the EU's advisory committee on mergers had recommended at a meeting on Tuesday that the deal should be cleared.</p>
<p>A final decision is expected probably on January 22.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6830</p>
</text>
